checkly:index/statusPageV3AutomationRule.description:
An automation rule of a v3 status page. When a check whose tags overlap with the rule's tags fails, Checkly opens one incident on the page impacting the listed components, and resolves it when the check recovers. Import uses the composite ID `<status_page_id>/<rule_id>`.

## Example Usage

<!--Start PulumiCodeChooser -->
```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as checkly from "@checkly/pulumi";

const example = new checkly.StatusPageV3("example", {
    name: "Example Application",
    url: "my-example-status-page",
});
const api = new checkly.StatusPageV3Component("api", {
    statusPageId: example.id,
    name: "API",
    displayOrder: 0,
});
// When a check tagged "api" fails, an incident is opened on the page marking
// the API component as a major outage, and resolved when the check recovers.
const apiOutage = new checkly.StatusPageV3AutomationRule("api_outage", {
    statusPageId: example.id,
    name: "API outage",
    firstUpdate: "We are investigating an issue with the API.",
    lastUpdate: "The issue has been resolved.",
    tags: ["api"],
    components: [{
        componentId: api.id,
        targetImpact: "MAJOR_OUTAGE",
    }],
});
```
